# Rails (Hotwire)

Coordinator and submitter UI for monthly close. Server-rendered HTML with Turbo. Add a Stimulus controller only for events, browser APIs, or client-only libraries.

Drive writer tokens, A1 unwrap, and SEFAZ mTLS stay on the server — never in views, Stimulus controllers, or frontend bundles.

## Files and names

- Directories and files: snake_case (`app/models/bank_account.rb`)
- Classes and modules: PascalCase; methods and symbols: snake_case
- Predicates end with `?` (`closed?`, `missing_document?`)
- Stimulus controllers: kebab-case filenames (`match_form_controller.js`)

## Ruby / Rails

- Rails 8 on MRI. Puma is the app server — not Node, not a separate API process
- Money: integer cents (`bigint` columns, Ruby `Integer`), never `Float` or `BigDecimal` for domain amounts
- Active Record for persistence. Keep queries out of views and Stimulus controllers
- Working files (photos, XML, statements) go through the blob/object-store interface, not durable writes under `Rails.root` or the container disk. Drive is only the **package archive** at **close-for-send**
- Tailwind for styling. Turbo/Stimulus for interactivity. No React, no shadcn/ui
- Semantic HTML, keyboard access, visible labels. Prefer buttons/links over clickable `div`s
- User-facing copy: Portuguese (Brazil), default locale `pt-BR`. Glossary: `CONTEXT.md`

```ruby
# BAD
Payment.all
amount.to_f

# GOOD
Current.organization.payments
amount_cents # Integer
```

## Access

- Operator session is Google OIDC (`openid email` only), not Drive
- Every query is scoped to the **Organization** of the current **Access**; never leak another organization’s rows
- A **Submitter** must not receive bank **Payment** or **Bank statement** data

## Tests (RSpec)

- Specs live in `spec/`. Do not skip, pending, or weaken examples to make a gate pass
- **Decision** (branch table, guard, state transition): prove at its own layer (model/job spec), one asserted case per enumerated member
- Code reached over HTTP: also a request spec at the boundary (status, who may call)
- Instrumentation / pass-through: no spec of its own — covered by the consumer
- System specs only when a check names a user-visible flow a request spec cannot settle
- Proofs name a specific example (`bin/rspec … -e "…"`), never the whole suite
